[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911272883","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105146#issuecomment-2911272883","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105146","id":2911272883,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6thn-z","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T06:32:34Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T06:32:34Z","body":"Is this something worth flagging on `DEBUG_ENABLED` as well (as `DEV_ASSERT` is only on dev builds)?\r\n\r\n(I'm not asking for change BTW, just your opinions.)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911272883/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911947712","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105146#issuecomment-2911947712","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105146","id":2911947712,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tkMvA","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T10:07:21Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T10:08:07Z","body":"> Is this something worth flagging on `DEBUG_ENABLED` as well (as `DEV_ASSERT` is only on dev builds)?\r\n> \r\n> (I'm not asking for change BTW, just your opinions.)\r\n\r\nGiven that this is checking for (rare) engine bugs, I opted to use `DEV_ASSERT`. But I wouldn't mind using `ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG` instead. The check should be pretty cheap either way.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2911947712/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912017037","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105146#issuecomment-2912017037","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105146","id":2912017037,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tkdqN","user":{"login":"lawnjelly","id":21999379,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIxOTk5Mzc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/21999379?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly","html_url":"https://github.com/lawnjelly","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/lawnjelly/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T10:32:32Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T10:32:32Z","body":"Maybe this might be better then:\r\n```\r\n#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED\r\nERR_FAIL_COND_MSG()\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\nor\r\n```\r\n#ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED\r\nif (cond)\r\n{\r\nERR_PRINT_ONCE();\r\nreturn BLAH;\r\n}\r\n#endif\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat way it will warn for anyone using the editor, won't slow down final exports, and won't stop people using the editor if they do discover a situation which spams this bug, e.g. creating circular reference in gdscript.\r\n\r\nI say this because `DEV_ASSERT()` is worth being a little careful with, it's more for something you are almost certain shouldn't happen, or preventing later PRs breaking existing code, because it can be annoying for DEV users as it is essentially a crash. If we have a bug in the wild we know will cause it already, there's a less convincing argument to make it assert.\r\n\r\nUnless we _do_ want it to crash to prevent data corruption, in which case even with `DEBUG_ENABLED` there might be an argument for `CRASH_NOW`.\r\n\r\nI wrote this comment in the `error_macro.h` a while back, as we had some problems with contributors overusing it. Generally the Godot paradigm it never crash, unless we _have to_:\r\n```\r\n * Note: IN MOST CASES YOU SHOULD NOT USE THIS MACRO.\r\n * Do not use unless you understand the trade-offs.\r\n *\r\n * DEV macros will be compiled out in releases, they are wrapped in DEV_ENABLED.\r\n *\r\n * Prefer WARNINGS / ERR_FAIL macros (which fail without crashing) - ERR_FAIL should be used in most cases.\r\n * Then CRASH_NOW_MSG macros (on rare occasions where error cannot be recovered).\r\n *\r\n * DEV_ASSERT should generally only be used when both of the following conditions are met:\r\n * 1) Bottleneck code where a check in release would be too expensive.\r\n * 2) Situations where the check would fail obviously and straight away during the maintenance of the code\r\n *    (i.e. strict conditions that should be true no matter what)\r\n *    and that can't fail for other contributors once the code is finished and merged.\r\n```","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912017037/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912030201","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105146#issuecomment-2912030201","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105146","id":2912030201,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tkg35","user":{"login":"Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce","html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-27T10:37:30Z","updated_at":"2025-05-27T10:37:30Z","body":"> Maybe this might be better then:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> #ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED\r\n> ERR_FAIL_COND_MSG()\r\n> #endif\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> or\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n> #ifdef DEBUG_ENABLED\r\n> if (cond)\r\n> {\r\n> ERR_PRINT_ONCE();\r\n> return BLAH;\r\n> }\r\n> #endif\r\n> ```\r\n> \r\n> That way it will warn for anyone using the editor, won't slow down final exports, and won't stop people using the editor if they do discover a situation which spams this bug, e.g. creating circular reference in gdscript.\r\n> \r\n> I say this because `DEV_ASSERT()` is worth being a little careful with, it's more for something you are almost certain shouldn't happen, or preventing later PRs breaking existing code, because it can be annoying for DEV users as it is essentially a crash. If we have a bug in the wild we know will cause it already, there's a less convincing argument to make it assert.\r\n> \r\n> Unless we _do_ want it to crash to prevent data corruption, in which case even with `DEBUG_ENABLED` there might be an argument for `CRASH_NOW`.\r\n> \r\n> I wrote this comment in the `error_macro.h` a while back, as we had some problems with contributors overusing it. Generally the Godot paradigm it never crash, unless we _have to_:\r\n> \r\n> ```\r\n>  * Note: IN MOST CASES YOU SHOULD NOT USE THIS MACRO.\r\n>  * Do not use unless you understand the trade-offs.\r\n>  *\r\n>  * DEV macros will be compiled out in releases, they are wrapped in DEV_ENABLED.\r\n>  *\r\n>  * Prefer WARNINGS / ERR_FAIL macros (which fail without crashing) - ERR_FAIL should be used in most cases.\r\n>  * Then CRASH_NOW_MSG macros (on rare occasions where error cannot be recovered).\r\n>  *\r\n>  * DEV_ASSERT should generally only be used when both of the following conditions are met:\r\n>  * 1) Bottleneck code where a check in release would be too expensive.\r\n>  * 2) Situations where the check would fail obviously and straight away during the maintenance of the code\r\n>  *    (i.e. strict conditions that should be true no matter what)\r\n>  *    and that can't fail for other contributors once the code is finished and merged.\r\n> ```\r\n\r\nThose are some good points.\r\nIn my own code I _would_ want to crash as this is an egregious affront that should be fixed asap.\r\nBut at the same time, some dev may run into it randomly without being responsible. So crashing could be annoying in this case.\r\nI'll go with your first suggestion, to make it a soft fail in DEBUG instead :)","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912030201/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2912264493","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105146#issuecomment-2912264493","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/105146","id":2912264493,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tlaEt","user":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.g